From a46b90fe77d866c751a32a10e339ba3d4b6ee036 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:42:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: USB format, dual-WAN backup, first-boot box, firewall
 fixes

- USB Format/Scan: the page set diskmon_usbport through start_apply,
  which validate_apply rewrites, so the port never reached rc; it now
  uses change_diskmon_unit and reads it back. start_diskformat no longer
  dereferences a missing disk; the scan says when a FAT/exFAT volume
  cannot be checked.
- rpunctd: stopped and started around restart_wireless and idle until
  the radios are ready (field: GT-BE98 wl2 dongle death on Dynamic).
- AiMesh "Ethernet Backhaul Mode" relabelled "Ethernet-Only Backhaul"
  (it disables the wireless fallback), 25 packs.
- Rules engine: the group/zone/zone-policy caps log once per ruleset and
  the page refuses them at save; the confirmed snapshot is staged in full
  before publishing, boot re-adopts an unmarked snapshot instead of
  blessing empty lists over it, and a failed save keeps the draft.
- Warden: rules restored in one iptables-restore --noflush batch per
  stack, per-rule fallback.
- Dual WAN: the Dashboard follows wan_primary; a connected backup WAN
  lights the WAN LED red and white, red alone when down.
- First-boot setup box: runs the SDN reconcile a guest-network apply
  runs (sync_apgx_to_wlunit before commit, restart_sdn in the chain), so
  the Network page's main card opens after a factory reset.
- Rule Status (reaper_fwsim 1.7): a rules-engine witness enters on the
  rule's own source zone and aims at its destination zone; VLAN-scoped
  rules were judged from br0. reaper_fwsim build outputs git-ignored.
- Diagnostics v1.3.24: roaming/scheduler/DFS/auth+PMF, roamast and radar
  counts, RAM log store with a USB disk present.
- New tokens RDST_78, RFW_323-325; 25 packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
